  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges, each equal to <math> <mrow> <mtext>q</mtext> </mrow> </math>, are kept at <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>&#160;=&#160;</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </math> on the x-axis. A particle of mass <math> <mrow> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </math> and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>q</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mtext>q</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; is placed at the origin. If charge <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>q</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> is given a small displacement <math> <mrow> <mtext>(y &#60;&#60; a)</mtext> </mrow> </math> along the y-axis, the net force acting on the particle is proportional to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>y</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
